{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310719,"nonce":"URT26jPT4eifSNDX2D+DFaWHxD4=","title":"case { b: 5 } never matches — the pattern lowers to an object LITERAL and the switch compares by reference. Needs a representational ...","message":"**`case { b: 5 }` never matches.** Verified minimal repro (parenthesised, so it\nis not the optional-paren switch work):\n\n```haxe\nvar o = { b: 5 };\nswitch (o) { case { b: 5 }: trace(\"ok\"); case _: trace(\"BAD\"); }   // prints BAD\n```\n\n**Root cause.** `ast_lowering/expr/patterns.rs` `lower_pattern_to_expression`,\n`Pattern::Object` arm, converts the pattern into a `TypedExpressionKind::\nObjectLiteral` — a freshly allocated `{ b: 5 }`. `expr/switch.rs` then stores it\nas `TypedSwitchCase.case_value` and the switch compares the scrutinee against\nit. Two separately allocated anonymous structures compare by REFERENCE, so the\ntest is always false.\n\nVariable binding for `case {i: extracted}` is handled separately and correctly\n(`bind_pattern_variables`, `Pattern::Object` arm) — it is only the match TEST\nthat is wrong.\n\n\n- Making `==` on anonymous structures structural would be WRONG: in Haxe\n  `{b:5} == {b:5}` is legitimately `false` (reference equality).\n- The pattern test must be field-wise (`scrutinee.b == 5 \u0026\u0026 ...`), and\n  `TypedSwitchCase` carries a single `case_value: TypedExpression`, which cannot\n  express a conjunction of field tests.\n\nSo the fix is a representational change to how a switch case carries its test,\nrippling into HIR/MIR switch lowering. Not a local edit.\n\n**Scope:** 13 corpus tests use `case {`. Related and also open, found alongside:\n`switch (cast x : T)` SIGSEGVs (reproduces with parentheses, so pre-existing and\nunrelated to the optional-paren change in 6dbf2611).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_structure_patterns_never_match` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}